INT. ROLLER RINK - AFTER CLOSING

Disco ball still turning. Chairs up on tables. Carpet-covered walls.

DEZ (16) sits on the skate counter in one rental skate. He holds the other. MARISOL (16) leans on the rail, arms crossed. TOBY (15) lies flat on the floor, staring at the ceiling.

DEZ
So that's it. Last night.

MARISOL
Dez, the rink is closing. Not you.

TOBY
It's basically you. You were born here.

DEZ
Rink rat. That's what Mr. Pruitt called me.

MARISOL
He called me that too.

TOBY
He called everyone that.

DEZ
My first kiss was by the snack bar.

MARISOL
It was me.

DEZ
It was a hot dog. I was kissing a hot dog.

TOBY
I was there. It was sad.

MARISOL
We'll find somewhere else.

DEZ
There isn't anywhere else.

TOBY
There's the parking lot.

MARISOL
The parking lot has no music.

TOBY
I'll bring a speaker.

He sits up. Grins. She lets her arms drop.

DEZ
Fine. Parking lot. Saturdays.

MARISOL
Saturdays.

Dez slides the second skate on. Stands. Wobbles. Rolls one slow lap, alone, while the ball keeps turning.
